        "original_id": "f82de4db-8d4d-5a6e-ad08-0db97539e253",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Damian Green\n- Concepts: Parliamentary privilege\n- Events: 2010 MPs expenses scandal, Damian Green arrest, super-injunction cases\n- Legal Cases: RJW & SJW v The Guardian newspaper & Person or Persons Unknown, CTB v News Group Newspapers\n- Roles: Member of Parliament for Ashford, First Secretary of State, Minister for the Cabinet Office\n\nFacts:\n- The doctrine of Parliamentary privilege was unsuccessfully used to try to prevent details of the 2010 MPs expenses scandal from emerging.\n- Damian Green was born on 17 January 1956.\n- Damian Green has been the Conservative Member of Parliament for Ashford since 1997.\n- In recent years, Parliamentary privilege made headlines in relation to the arrest of Damian Green and super-injunction cases including RJW & SJW v The Guardian newspaper & Person or Persons Unknown and CTB v News Group Newspapers.\n- The headlines involving Parliamentary privilege led to calls to reform the law relating to privilege.\n- Damian Green has served as First Secretary of State and Minister for the Cabinet Office since 11 June 2017.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "c82f1a94-6dcc-5609-9877-dbf56cee73a2",
        "text": "Page: Parliamentary privilege in the United Kingdom. Sentence: The doctrine of Parliamentary privilege was unsuccessfully used to try and prevent details of 2010 MPs expenses scandal from emerging.\nPage: Parliamentary privilege in the United Kingdom. Sentence: In recent years the doctrine of Parliamentary privilege has made headlines in relation to the arrest of Damian Green and several cases relating to super-injunctions such as \"RJW & SJW v The Guardian newspaper & Person or Persons Unknown\" ('Trafigura') and \"CTB v News Group Newspapers\" leading to calls to reform the law relating to privilege.\nPage: Damian Green. Sentence: Damian Howard Green (born 17 January 1956) is a British politician who has been the Conservative Member of Parliament for Ashford since 1997 and the First Secretary of State and Minister for the Cabinet Office since 11 June 2017.",
